---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---
<Base title={`About Me | ${site.name}`}>
  <div class="proj-head"><h1>About Me</h1></div>
  <article class="prose">
    <div class="about-top">
  <img class="portrait" src="/media/fairshots/ShreyasAbout.jpeg" alt="Shreyas Shejwal" width="640" height="480" />
  <div>
    <p>I'm Shreyas, a game developer studying for a BCA in Game Development at Ajeenkya DY Patil University, Pune (graduating <code>TODO year</code>). I work mostly in Unity with C#, and I also write C++.</p>
    <p>I think making games is art, and the best part of any art is when someone understands it and enjoys it. A game is the one medium where people don't only look at your work, they play it. That is what I'm after: something people have fun with and remember.</p>
  </div>
</div>
    <h2>What shapes how I design</h2>
    <p>Contra and Super Contra, A Way Out and Helldivers taught me how good a game feels when two people share it. Florence showed me that a game can be about feeling something instead of winning. GTA and Minecraft are systems that give players room to make their own stories. I try to build the second kind of thing, with the warmth of the first.</p>
    <h2>What I do on a team</h2>
<p>I design and build gameplay systems. I take a mechanic from an idea to a working prototype, then make it solid enough that the rest of the team can build on it. I'm comfortable on both sides of that handoff: designing the rules and writing the code that runs them.</p>
<p>I'm most useful where a game needs its structure worked out: how systems connect, what the player should feel, and how to explain that clearly to artists, programmers and designers.</p>
    <h2>Get in touch</h2>
    <p>{site.status}. Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>, or find me on {site.links.map((l, i) => <><a href={l.url} rel="noopener">{l.label}</a>{i < site.links.length - 1 ? ' or ' : '.'}</>)}</p>
    {site.resume ? <p><a href={site.resume}>Download my resume (PDF)</a></p> : <p class="todo">Resume link goes here once you add resume.pdf (see src/data/site.ts).</p>}
  </article>
</Base>
